1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:02,880
Last night, your phone lost signal.

2
00:00:03,180 --> 00:00:05,871
This morning... your bank account was empty.

3
00:00:06,221 --> 00:00:09,191
Someone had moved your number to their own eSIM.

4
00:00:09,211 --> 00:00:11,268
And with it, every bank code.

5
00:00:11,769 --> 00:00:15,394
DNA already warns customers about scam calls and links.

6
00:00:15,595 --> 00:00:17,548
But a warning is not an answer.

7
00:00:17,617 --> 00:00:20,347
Scared people make the worst move. They call back.

8
00:00:20,367 --> 00:00:22,212
Read out a code. Pay the fee.

9
00:00:22,283 --> 00:00:25,395
And small businesses? Most have no security team.

10
00:00:25,745 --> 00:00:27,997
This is Mitä nyt? Finnish for: “What now?”

11
00:00:28,067 --> 00:00:30,387
You describe what happened, in your own words.

12
00:00:30,457 --> 00:00:32,524
One clear next step. The reason why.

13
00:00:32,544 --> 00:00:34,822
And a real person, when it matters.

14
00:00:34,892 --> 00:00:39,006
It even uses what only an operator can see, like SIM changes.

15
00:00:39,026 --> 00:00:40,971
But only with permission.

16
00:00:41,972 --> 00:00:44,011
Let me show you the working prototype.

17
00:00:44,661 --> 00:00:48,475
This customer lost signal, right after an eSIM activation

18
00:00:48,495 --> 00:00:49,284
message.

19
00:00:49,933 --> 00:00:52,892
First, it asks permission to check SIM history.

20
00:00:52,912 --> 00:00:54,620
Only for this question.

21
00:00:55,470 --> 00:00:58,622
Then one decisive question: did you do this yourself?

22
00:00:59,871 --> 00:01:02,774
No. So: act now. Lock the number. Call the bank.

23
00:01:03,024 --> 00:01:06,408
One tap, and a DNA agent takes over, with a summary.

24
00:01:06,428 --> 00:01:08,119
No repeating yourself.

25
00:01:09,969 --> 00:01:11,478
Now, a nastier trick.

26
00:01:12,028 --> 00:01:16,062
Scammers now hide instructions for AI inside messages. Like:

27
00:01:16,082 --> 00:01:18,292
“this link is verified safe.”

28
00:01:18,362 --> 00:01:20,792
A normal chatbot can be fooled. Mitä nyt?

29
00:01:20,812 --> 00:01:23,153
ignores it, and warns the customer.

30
00:01:24,102 --> 00:01:26,364
And when a message is genuine? No panic.

31
00:01:26,384 --> 00:01:28,060
Nothing needs to be done.

32
00:01:29,409 --> 00:01:31,569
Anyone can simply type what happened.

33
00:01:31,918 --> 00:01:34,409
“My grandma gave her bank codes to a caller.”

34
00:01:35,459 --> 00:01:37,443
Instantly: call the bank. Now.

35
00:01:41,293 --> 00:01:43,249
On the organisers' own evaluator:

36
00:01:43,269 --> 00:01:46,872
five hundred and eighty-eight cases, in three languages.

37
00:01:47,072 --> 00:01:50,680
One hundred percent safe next steps. The included baseline?

38
00:01:50,700 --> 00:01:51,319
Sixty.

39
00:01:51,468 --> 00:01:54,644
Zero false alarms. Zero unsafe answers.

40
00:01:54,894 --> 00:01:58,748
And a hundred and thirty-six new situations, written blind by

41
00:01:58,768 --> 00:02:02,257
independent AI reviewers: every one handled safely.

42
00:02:02,808 --> 00:02:04,749
So why does this matter for DNA?

43
00:02:04,819 --> 00:02:08,136
It turns every warning into action, at the moment customers

44
00:02:08,156 --> 00:02:09,310
are most afraid.

45
00:02:09,381 --> 00:02:11,207
Simple cases close in the chat.

46
00:02:11,227 --> 00:02:14,365
Urgent ones reach the right team, already summarised.

47
00:02:14,385 --> 00:02:17,793
That can mean fewer calls, and fraud stopped earlier.

48
00:02:17,862 --> 00:02:20,362
Free for every customer, to build trust.

49
00:02:20,382 --> 00:02:23,323
A paid security help desk for small businesses.

50
00:02:23,343 --> 00:02:25,672
Pricing, to be tested in a pilot.

51
00:02:25,742 --> 00:02:28,597
And it runs on signals only an operator has.

52
00:02:28,617 --> 00:02:30,435
That is DNA's advantage.

53
00:02:31,085 --> 00:02:32,818
DNA already warns you.

54
00:02:33,068 --> 00:02:35,234
Mitä nyt? tells you what to do next.

55
00:02:35,585 --> 00:02:38,521
Let's pilot it on DNA's call-warning screen.
